sequenceDiagram
    participant U as User
    participant PD as Processes Dashboard
    participant FS as File Service
    participant API as Backend API
    participant PS as Process Service
    participant IS as Integration Service
    participant VS as Validation Service
    participant DB as Database

    Note over U, PD: Process export workflow
    U->>PD: Access processes dashboard
    PD->>U: Display existing processes
    U->>PD: Right-click on "Weekly Newsletter Campaign"
    PD->>U: Show context menu
    U->>PD: Select "Export Process"
    
    PD->>API: GET /api/processes/{id}/export
    API->>PS: Fetch complete process configuration
    PS->>DB: Get process details, integrations, settings
    DB->>PS: Return process data
    PS->>API: Return exportable process
    API->>FS: Generate export file
    FS->>FS: Create JSON export package
    FS->>API: Export file ready
    API->>PD: Return download link
    PD->>U: Trigger file download "newsletter_campaign.json"
    
    Note over U, PD: Process import workflow
    U->>PD: Click "Import Process" button
    PD->>U: Open file upload dialog
    U->>FS: Select process file "marketing_automation.json"
    FS->>PD: File selected
    PD->>U: Show import preview dialog
    
    PD->>FS: POST /api/files/upload
    FS->>VS: Validate file format
    VS->>FS: File format valid
    FS->>API: Process import file
    API->>PS: Parse process configuration
    PS->>VS: Validate process structure
    VS->>PS: Process structure valid
    PS->>API: Process ready for import
    API->>PD: Return import preview
    
    PD->>U: Show import summary
    PD->>U: Display process name "Marketing Automation Template"
    PD->>U: Display required integrations list
    PD->>U: Show department "Marketing"
    PD->>U: Show priority "High"
    
    Note over PD: Integration compatibility check
    PD->>IS: GET /api/integrations/check-compatibility
    IS->>IS: Check required vs available integrations
    IS->>PD: Return compatibility report
    PD->>U: Show integration status
    PD->>U: Display " Mailchimp - Available"
    PD->>U: Display " Canva - Available"
    PD->>U: Display " Adobe Creative - Not connected"
    PD->>U: Display " Salesforce - Not available"
    
    Note over U, PD: Handle missing integrations
    U->>PD: Click "Configure Missing Integrations"
    PD->>IS: GET /api/integrations/alternatives
    IS->>PD: Return alternative integrations
    PD->>U: Show integration alternatives
    PD->>U: Suggest "HubSpot" instead of "Salesforce"
    
    U->>PD: Select "HubSpot" as alternative
    U->>PD: Click "Skip Adobe Creative for now"
    PD->>IS: Update integration mapping
    IS->>PD: Mapping updated
    
    Note over U, PD: Process customization
    U->>PD: Click "Customize Before Import"
    PD->>U: Show customization form
    U->>PD: Change process name to "Q2 Marketing Campaign"
    U->>PD: Update department to "Marketing"
    U->>PD: Keep priority as "High"
    U->>PD: Modify process description
    
    Note over U, PD: Import execution
    U->>PD: Click "Import Process"
    PD->>API: POST /api/processes/import
    API->>PS: Create process from import data
    PS->>DB: Save imported process
    DB->>PS: Process created with new ID
    PS->>IS: Configure selected integrations
    IS->>PS: Integrations configured
    PS->>API: Import completed
    API->>PD: Import successful
    
    PD->>U: Show import success message
    PD->>U: Display "Process imported successfully"
    PD->>PD: Refresh processes table
    PD->>U: Show imported process with "Imported" badge
    
    Note over U, PD: Bulk export workflow
    U->>PD: Select multiple processes
    U->>PD: Click "Bulk Actions" dropdown
    PD->>U: Show bulk options
    U->>PD: Select "Export Selected"
    
    PD->>API: POST /api/processes/bulk-export
    API->>PS: Fetch multiple processes
    
    loop For each selected process
        PS->>DB: Get process configuration
        DB->>PS: Return process data
    end
    
    PS->>API: Return all process data
    API->>FS: Create bulk export package
    FS->>FS: Generate ZIP file with multiple JSON files
    FS->>API: Bulk export ready
    API->>PD: Return download link
    PD->>U: Download "processes_export.zip"
    
    Note over U, PD: Bulk import workflow
    U->>PD: Click "Import Process"
    U->>FS: Select ZIP file "department_processes.zip"
    FS->>PD: Multiple files detected
    PD->>U: Show bulk import dialog
    
    PD->>FS: Extract and validate files
    FS->>VS: Validate each process file
    VS->>FS: All files valid
    FS->>PD: Show import queue
    PD->>U: Display "5 processes ready for import"
    
    U->>PD: Review each process summary
    U->>PD: Deselect "Legacy Process" 
    U->>PD: Click "Import Selected (4 processes)"
    
    PD->>API: POST /api/processes/bulk-import
    
    loop For each selected process
        API->>PS: Create process
        PS->>DB: Save process
        PS->>IS: Configure integrations
    end
    
    API->>PD: Bulk import completed
    PD->>U: Show "4 processes imported, 1 skipped"
    PD->>U: Refresh dashboard with new processes 